{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01BnEnf7vhAd1KTaPZ8VRXQj","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# ADR-005 — External-Service Verification Policy\n2\t\n3\t**Status:** Accepted · 2026-07-18 · Owner: User (governance), Architect (technical)\n4\t\n5\t## Decision\n6\t\n7\tNo ticket may require **live external verification** as its only acceptance path unless\n8\tthe required credentials and environment are explicitly available to the executor.\n9\tEvery ticket that touches an external service (Google OAuth, Apps Script runtime,\n10\t`clasp`, real Sheets workbooks, bank portals, WhatsApp Business API, or any production\n11\tcredential) must define two separate acceptance tiers:\n12\t\n13\t1. **Local acceptance criteria** — files created/modified, static validation, schema\n14\t   validation, mocked/dry-run behavior, documentation updated, deterministic tests that\n15\t   need no credentials.\n16\t2. **Live verification criteria** — exact external account/service required, required\n17\t   credentials, required command, expected live result, manual fallback if automation\n18\t   is unavailable.\n19\t\n20\tIf local implementation is complete but live verification cannot run (missing\n21\tcredentials/access), the executor must **not** report the ticket as failed. Correct\n22\tstatus: `completed-local / pending-live-verification` — or, if the dashboard's ledger\n23\tonly supports its existing four states, `blocked` with blocker type\n24\t`blocked-external-verification`.\n25\t\n26\tExecutor must report explicitly: what was completed locally; what was not verified\n27\tlive; which credential/service/workbook/command/account is missing; the exact next\n28\tverification step for a human or a properly provisioned agent. External-verification\n29\tblockage must never trigger unnecessary code rewrites or re-implementation attempts.\n30\t\n31\t## Context\n32\t\n33\tExecutor agents run in local/sandboxed environments without Google OAuth, Apps Script\n34\truntime, `clasp`, real Sheets workbooks, bank portals, WhatsApp Business API access, or\n35\tproduction credentials. Prior to this ADR, tickets like INF-001 (Sheets Workbook\n36\tBootstrap) had no explicit split between \"script written and internally correct\" and\n37\t\"script actually run against a real Google Sheet\" — risk of an executor either (a)\n38\tfalsely claiming full completion for work only locally validated, or (b) burning cycles\n39\trewriting already-correct code because it can't complete live verification it was never\n40\tprovisioned to do.\n41\t\n42\t## Consequences\n43\t\n44\t1. Every open/future ticket touching an external service gets its acceptance criteria\n45\t   split into the two tiers above. Existing tickets are retrofitted (see Propagation).\n46\t2. Dashboard ledger's `blocked` state gains a documented blocker-type convention;\n47\t   `blocked-external-verification` specifically means \"code/local work may be done,\n48\t   external step needs credentials/human,\" distinct from `blocked` for a genuine\n49\t   spec/business blocker (e.g. FIX-002's old permission-sandbox confusion must not\n50\t   recur under a different name).\n51\t3. Architect (acceptance review) must check the local tier independently (as already\n52\t   practiced — reading files, running static checks) and treat live-tier gaps as\n53\t   expected, not as grounds for rejecting the ticket, provided the executor's report\n54\t   correctly names the missing credential/service and next step.\n55\t4. Does not change who *holds* credentials — DIS-001/DIS-003 (human tasks) remain the\n56\t   path by which real Google Workspace access, bank portal access, and WhatsApp\n57\t   Business API access get provisioned. This ADR only governs how tickets are scoped\n58\t   and accepted while that access is pending.\n59\t\n60\t## Propagation status (2026-07-18)\n61\t\n62\tApplied to INF-001 (Sheets Workbook Bootstrap), INF-002 (Apps Script Web App Skeleton),\n63\tINF-003, INT-001/INT-002 (LEPTON/KDT export), and payment-evidence-touching tickets\n64\t(APP-005 and related). Each retrofitted with explicit local vs. live acceptance tiers\n65\tper this ADR — see `roadmap.md` ticket bodies for the per-ticket split.\n66\t\n67\t2026-07-18 (later same day): also retrofitted FIX-004 (runner/model selection reset by\n68\tpoll) — its live tier requires an interactive browser session and real wall-clock 4s\n69\tpoll cycles, an executor-environment capability gap treated as external verification\n70\tunder this policy even though no credential is involved. Ledger correction notes in\n71\t`roadmap-status.md` (2026-07-18T14:31:14Z) reclassified INF-001 and FIX-004 as\n72\t`blocked` / `blocked-external-verification`. Enforcement ticket GOV-002 (relaunch gate:\n73\tno relaunch of `blocked-external-verification` tickets without explicit human\n74\tacknowledgment + reason) added to `roadmap.md` after repeated no-op relaunches of both\n75\ttickets demonstrated the process gap.\n76\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"91096542-237d-4741-963c-17e41dadf228","uuid":"d50da515-9434-48a1-8fca-2dd5c16a1705","timestamp":"2026-07-18T15:20:42.188Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/work945/Documents/Proyectos/ABM/proyectos/panel-ops/docs/adr/ADR-005-external-verification-policy.md","content":"# ADR-005 — External-Service Verification Policy\n\n**Status:** Accepted · 2026-07-18 · Owner: User (governance), Architect (technical)\n\n## Decision\n\nNo ticket may require **live external verification** as its only acceptance path unless\nthe required credentials and environment are explicitly available to the executor.\nEvery ticket that touches an external service (Google OAuth, Apps Script runtime,\n`clasp`, real Sheets workbooks, bank portals, WhatsApp Business API, or any production\ncredential) must define two separate acceptance tiers:\n\n1. **Local acceptance criteria** — files created/modified, static validation, schema\n   validation, mocked/dry-run behavior, documentation updated, deterministic tests that\n   need no credentials.\n2. **Live verification criteria** — exact external account/service required, required\n   credentials, required command, expected live result, manual fallback if automation\n   is unavailable.\n\nIf local implementation is complete but live verification cannot run (missing\ncredentials/access), the executor must **not** report the ticket as failed. Correct\nstatus: `completed-local / pending-live-verification` — or, if the dashboard's ledger\nonly supports its existing four states, `blocked` with blocker type\n`blocked-external-verification`.\n\nExecutor must report explicitly: what was completed locally; what was not verified\nlive; which credential/service/workbook/command/account is missing; the exact next\nverification step for a human or a properly provisioned agent. External-verification\nblockage must never trigger unnecessary code rewrites or re-implementation attempts.\n\n## Context\n\nExecutor agents run in local/sandboxed environments without Google OAuth, Apps Script\nruntime, `clasp`, real Sheets workbooks, bank portals, WhatsApp Business API access, or\nproduction credentials. Prior to this ADR, tickets like INF-001 (Sheets Workbook\nBootstrap) had no explicit split between \"script written and internally correct\" and\n\"script actually run against a real Google Sheet\" — risk of an executor either (a)\nfalsely claiming full completion for work only locally validated, or (b) burning cycles\nrewriting already-correct code because it can't complete live verification it was never\nprovisioned to do.\n\n## Consequences\n\n1. Every open/future ticket touching an external service gets its acceptance criteria\n   split into the two tiers above. Existing tickets are retrofitted (see Propagation).\n2. Dashboard ledger's `blocked` state gains a documented blocker-type convention;\n   `blocked-external-verification` specifically means \"code/local work may be done,\n   external step needs credentials/human,\" distinct from `blocked` for a genuine\n   spec/business blocker (e.g. FIX-002's old permission-sandbox confusion must not\n   recur under a different name).\n3. Architect (acceptance review) must check the local tier independently (as already\n   practiced — reading files, running static checks) and treat live-tier gaps as\n   expected, not as grounds for rejecting the ticket, provided the executor's report\n   correctly names the missing credential/service and next step.\n4. Does not change who *holds* credentials — DIS-001/DIS-003 (human tasks) remain the\n   path by which real Google Workspace access, bank portal access, and WhatsApp\n   Business API access get provisioned. This ADR only governs how tickets are scoped\n   and accepted while that access is pending.\n\n## Propagation status (2026-07-18)\n\nApplied to INF-001 (Sheets Workbook Bootstrap), INF-002 (Apps Script Web App Skeleton),\nINF-003, INT-001/INT-002 (LEPTON/KDT export), and payment-evidence-touching tickets\n(APP-005 and related). Each retrofitted with explicit local vs. live acceptance tiers\nper this ADR — see `roadmap.md` ticket bodies for the per-ticket split.\n\n2026-07-18 (later same day): also retrofitted FIX-004 (runner/model selection reset by\npoll) — its live tier requires an interactive browser session and real wall-clock 4s\npoll cycles, an executor-environment capability gap treated as external verification\nunder this policy even though no credential is involved. Ledger correction notes in\n`roadmap-status.md` (2026-07-18T14:31:14Z) reclassified INF-001 and FIX-004 as\n`blocked` / `blocked-external-verification`. Enforcement ticket GOV-002 (relaunch gate:\nno relaunch of `blocked-external-verification` tickets without explicit human\nacknowledgment + reason) added to `roadmap.md` after repeated no-op relaunches of both\ntickets demonstrated the process gap.\n","numLines":76,"startLine":1,"totalLines":76}}}
